    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d230-a4-a3">

                <pb facs="0578" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg492"/>

                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. B. M’s
                            Legation and Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 11, 1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received with unfeigned sorrow your
                    excellency’s dispatch of this date, announcing the decease of His late Majesty
                    Kamehameha V.</p>
                <p>I shall communicate the melancholy information to Her Majesty’s government, and I
                    am assured that the intelligence will be received by Her Majesty Queen Victoria
                    with profound grief.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, with the highest consideration, your excellency’s
                    obedient humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THEO. H. DAVIES.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. W. Hutchison</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs, &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
